    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45062" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐρύ̆-χορος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with broad places,
			spacious</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μυκαλησσός,
			Λακεδαίμων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.498
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.1
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἑλλάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.478
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτόλις</span>, of Troy, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				20a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσία, Λιβύα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				7.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				4.43
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄργος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					9.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγυιαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					8.55
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				87
			</span></i> (lyr.), Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.52
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.319
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Nicod.
			</span></i>). (Prop.<i>with broad dancing-places</i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορός</span>; then a conventional epithet,
			perh. connected by poets with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῶρος.</span>)</div>
